.TH MAILFIRE 1 "October 16, 2026" "mailfire" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mailfire \- send email from the command line via the Mailgun API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mailfire
.RB [ send ]
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B mailfire validate
.RB [ \-c
.IR path ]
.br
.B mailfire resend
.RB [ \-\-list " | " \-\-force " | " \fIid\fR...]
.RB [ \-c
.IR path ]
.br
.B mailfire version
.br
.B mailfire
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mailfire
is a client for the Mailgun HTTP API that sends email from the command line.
The message body is read from standard input, or from a file with
.BR \-\-file .
Plain text, Markdown, and HTML bodies are supported; Markdown and HTML
are rendered into a built-in, responsive email template.
.PP
Without a subcommand,
.B send
is assumed.
On success the Mailgun message ID is printed to standard output.
.PP
If sending fails because of a network error, a Mailgun server error, or rate
limiting, the composed message is stored for later retrying with
.B mailfire resend
(unless deferral is disabled).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B send
Compose and send an email.
This is the default subcommand.
.TP
.B validate
Check, step by step, that the configuration file is found and valid TOML,
that all mandatory keys are well-formed, and that the API key and domain are
accepted by Mailgun.
No mail is sent.
.TP
.B resend
Retry deferred messages, oldest first.
A message is removed only after successful delivery.
Messages deferred less than
.B resend_cooldown
ago are skipped unless
.B \-\-force
is given.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, commit, and build date.
.PP
Every subcommand accepts
.BR \-h " and " \-\-help .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Flags of send
.TP
.BI \-\-to " addr"
Recipient, repeatable.
Required, at least once.
Accepts
.B user@example.com
or
.BR "Name <user@example.com>" .
Comma-separated lists are not supported, because commas are legal in display names.
.TP
.BI \-\-cc " addr"
Carbon copy recipient, repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-bcc " addr"
Blind carbon copy recipient, repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-from " addr"
Sender; overrides the
.B from
setting of the configuration file.
Required if the configuration file does not set
.BR from .
.TP
.BI \-\-subject " text"
Subject line.
Required.
.TP
.B \-\-txt
Body is plain text.
This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-md
Body is Markdown, rendered into the built-in template.
A plain-text alternative is sent as well.
Local images referenced as
.B ![alt](path/to/image.png)
are attached and displayed inline; remote image URLs are left untouched.
.TP
.B \-\-html
Body is an HTML fragment, wrapped in the built-in template.
.TP
.B \-\-html\-raw
Body is a complete HTML document, sent as-is.
.PP
Exactly one of the four body format flags may be given.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " path"
Read the body from a file instead of standard input.
.TP
.BI \-\-preheader " text"
Hidden inbox preview text.
Only with
.B \-\-md
or
.BR \-\-html .
.TP
.BI \-\-footer " path"
HTML fragment appended as footer.
Only with
.B \-\-md
or
.BR \-\-html .
.TP
.BI \-\-attach " path"
Attach a file, repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-test
Use Mailgun test mode: the API validates the request, but nothing is delivered.
Test sends are never deferred.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-defer
Fail immediately instead of storing the message for a later resend.
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-config " path"
Use this configuration file instead of searching the default locations.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SS Flags of resend
.TP
.B \-\-list
Show deferred messages (ID, date, to, subject, size) without sending.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Resend even messages younger than the cooldown.
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-config " path"
Use this configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.PP
Without further arguments all eligible deferred messages are retried;
with one or more
.I id
arguments only those messages are retried.
.B \-\-list
cannot be combined with IDs.
.SS Flags of validate
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-config " path"
Use this configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B mailfire
reads a TOML configuration file.
The first existing file of the following locations is used:
.PP
Linux and macOS:
.RS
.nf
\&./.mailfire.conf
$HOME/.config/mailfire/mailfire.conf
/etc/mailfire/mailfire.conf
.fi
.RE
.PP
Windows:
.RS
.nf
\&.\e.mailfire.conf
%APPDATA%\emailfire\emailfire.conf
%PROGRAMDATA%\emailfire\emailfire.conf
.fi
.RE
.PP
The option
.B \-\-config
overrides the search.
Strings must be quoted.
On Linux and macOS a warning is printed when the file is accessible by group
or others; fix it with
.BR "chmod 600" .
.PP
A system-wide configuration is usually insecure, because anyone who can read
it can use the API key.
.SS [mailgun]
.TP
.B api_key
String, mandatory.
The Mailgun API key.
.TP
.B region
String, mandatory.
Either
.B us
or
.BR eu .
.SS [sending]
.TP
.B domain
String, mandatory.
The sending domain as configured at Mailgun.
.TP
.B from
String, optional.
Default sender, either
.B user@example.com
or
.BR "My Name <user@example.com>" .
Can be overridden with
.BR \-\-from .
If not set,
.B \-\-from
is mandatory.
.SS [logging]
.TP
.B logfile
String, optional.
Logging is disabled unless a logfile is given.
One JSON object per sending attempt is written per line.
.TP
.B loglevel
String, optional, default
.BR information .
.RS
.TP
.B error
Failed attempts only: time, message ID, recipients, status code.
.TP
.B information
Time, message ID, recipients, subject, status code.
.TP
.B debug
Time, message ID, sender, recipients, subject, message size, status code,
API response body.
.RE
.TP
.B max_size
String, optional, default
.BR 50M .
When exceeded, the oldest log lines are removed.
Accepts a number of bytes or a K, M, or G suffix.
.SS [defer]
.TP
.B defer
Boolean, optional, default
.BR true .
Store messages whose delivery failed for a later retry.
.TP
.B defer_dir
String, optional.
Directory for deferred messages; created on demand.
Defaults to
.I $HOME/.local/share/mailfire
(\fI%LOCALAPPDATA%\emailfire\fR on Windows).
.TP
.B max_size
String, optional, default
.BR 50M .
When exceeded, the oldest deferred messages are removed.
.TP
.B resend_cooldown
Duration string, optional, default
.BR 5m .
Messages younger than this are skipped by
.BR "mailfire resend" .
.SS Example
.nf
[mailgun]
  api_key = "<your-api-key>"
  region = "eu"

[sending]
  domain = "example.com"
  from = "My Name <user@example.com>"

[logging]
  logfile = "~/logs/mailfire.log"
  loglevel = "information"
  max_size = "100M"

[defer]
  defer = true
  max_size = "100M"
  resend_cooldown = "5m"
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (sent, validated, resent, or information shown).
.TP
.B 1
Usage error: missing flags, unknown subcommand, conflicting formats.
.TP
.B 2
Configuration error: missing file, invalid TOML, missing or invalid keys.
.TP
.B 3
Authentication error: the API key was rejected (401 or 403 from Mailgun).
.TP
.B 4
Sending failed and the message was deferred for a later
.BR "mailfire resend" .
.TP
.B 5
Sending failed and the message was not deferred
.RB ( \-\-no\-defer
or
.BR "defer = false" ).
.PP
Errors are written to standard error in plain language, naming the failing step.
.SH EXAMPLES
Send a Markdown message from standard input:
.PP
.nf
mailfire \-\-md \-\-to user@example.com \-\-subject "Have a nice day" <<EOF
# This is an Email

It is written in markdown. It's delivered as HTML.
EOF
.fi
.PP
Send files as attachments:
.PP
.nf
mailfire \-\-to user@example.com \-\-subject "The files" \e
  \-\-attach ~/doc1.pdf \-\-attach ~/image.png
.fi
.PP
Verify configuration and payload without delivering anything:
.PP
.nf
mailfire \-\-test \-\-to user@example.com \-\-subject "Test" <<< "Hello"
.fi
.PP
Check configuration and credentials:
.PP
.nf
mailfire validate
.fi
.PP
List, then retry deferred messages:
.PP
.nf
mailfire resend \-\-list
mailfire resend
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./.mailfire.conf
.TQ
.I $HOME/.config/mailfire/mailfire.conf
.TQ
.I /etc/mailfire/mailfire.conf
Configuration file locations on Linux and macOS, in search order.
.TP
.I %APPDATA%\emailfire\emailfire.conf
.TQ
.I %PROGRAMDATA%\emailfire\emailfire.conf
Configuration file locations on Windows, after
.IR .\e.mailfire.conf .
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/share/mailfire
Default directory for deferred messages
.RI ( %LOCALAPPDATA%\emailfire
on Windows).
.SH SEE ALSO
Project home and full documentation:
.UR https://github.com/thorstenkramm/mailfire
.UE
